------------------------------------------------------------------INTERVIEW DEFINITIONS------------------------------------------------

1. What is Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)
Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) is a programming paradigm that organizes software using objects. It is based on four fundamental 
principles: Encapsulation, Abstraction, Inheritance, and Polymorphism, which help build modular, reusable, and maintainable applications.


2. Object
An object is a real-time instance of a class that occupies memory and can access the properties and behaviors defined in the class.


3.class
A class is a blueprint or template used to create objects. It defines the properties (fields) and behaviors (methods) of an object.


